    <string name="shizuku_tutorial_title">Pair with a wireless debugging code</string>
    <string name="shizuku_tutorial_intro">For Android 11 and newer. Keep the phone connected to Wi-Fi and use split screen so Settings and Shizuku/Shevery can remain visible together.</string>
    <string name="shizuku_tutorial_step_1">Enable Developer options, then enable USB debugging and Wireless debugging.</string>
    <string name="shizuku_tutorial_step_2">Open Wireless debugging and tap “Pair device with pairing code”. Keep the six-digit code on screen.</string>
    <string name="shizuku_tutorial_step_3">Return to Shizuku/Shevery, choose pairing by code, enter the displayed code, and confirm.</string>
    <string name="shizuku_tutorial_step_4">Tap Start in Shizuku/Shevery. Return to MTZ Studio and allow its Shizuku permission request.</string>
    <string name="shizuku_tutorial_miui_tip">Xiaomi tip: the steps above are sufficient for normal pairing. Only if authorization fails and your device exposes it, enable “USB debugging (Security settings)”. Restart the service after every phone reboot.</string>
